(version 1)

# Fab capabilities that KiCad has no board-wide setting for, taken from the
# cited profile fab-profiles/jlcpcb-2layer-1oz.json. See ADR-0006.
#
# Every rule here has been proven to evaluate, not merely to parse: a rule
# that parses and never matches is worse than no rule, because it reads as
# coverage. The method is to set the threshold absurdly, confirm DRC reports
# the violation and names the rule, then restore.

# JLCPCB Drilling: "Min. Non-plated holes 0.50mm".
# Verified live: at min 5.0mm this reports
#   [drill_out_of_range] ... (rule 'npth_min_hole' min hole 5.0000 mm; actual 2.2000 mm)
# against both mounting holes, and matches no SMD pad.
(rule "npth_min_hole"
	(constraint hole_size (min 0.50mm))
	(condition "A.Pad_Type == 'NPTH, mechanical'")
)

# NOT ENCODED: JLCPCB "NPTH pad annular ring >= 0.45mm".
#
# A rule using (constraint annular_width) with the same NPTH condition parses
# cleanly and never fires -- set to min 9.0mm against holes whose annulus is
# 0.00mm (pad size 2.2mm == drill 2.2mm), DRC reported nothing. KiCad 10.0.5
# does not appear to evaluate annular_width for NPTH pads.
#
# The vendor figure applies to NPTH pads that carry copper; plain mounting
# holes have none. Rather than ship a rule that reads as coverage and provides
# none, this is left to a human check when a copper-ringed NPTH pad first
# appears on a board here.
